# Multi-line body integrity check

The integrity field above declares the expected digest of the canonical
body bytes. A conforming loader rejects this fixture unless the digest
matches the recomputed value at load time.

This sample exercises three body-content shapes in one document:

1. Plain paragraph text
2. A fenced code block
3. A trailing paragraph after the fence

```ts
import { loadMdaConfig } from '@snoai/mda-config';

const cfg = await loadMdaConfig(path, { verifyIntegrity: true });
```

Trailing paragraph included to ensure the canonicalizer handles
body content after a fence boundary correctly.
